# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 2.8633e+05 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 0.8580 85.420 3.9220e+06 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~85 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 3.3510 42.946 3.8183e+09 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 1 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 3.4082 41.975 1.1190e+10 stylized  Light rises x19.8 in 0.18 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 42.9 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 41.2 km (98% of m0); yield gen 1 at 40.1 km (37% of m0). Dust groups supply 80% of the rise and 76% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 3.4500 41.265 2.1524e+10 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x5.6 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 F flare 3.6051 38.672 9.9146e+10 stylized  Light rises x1.3 in 0.06 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: split gen 1 at 38.4 km (36% of m0); yield gen 1 at 38.2 km (18% of m0). Dust groups supply 65% of the rise and 59% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
7 b bump 3.7797 35.805 1.9644e+11 stylized  Small fluctuation, 47% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 1) at 35.6 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
8 P peak 3.7881 35.668 2.0404e+11 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+1.9 km from the peak of energy deposition (33.8 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 18.1 km/s).
9 - drag_overtakes_ablation 4.0734 31.518 8.0679e+10 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
10 D rolloff 4.0824 31.410 7.5038e+10 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.29 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 71% of v0, 38% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
11 R retirement_step 4.8356 25.369 5.0781e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 19% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
12 R retirement_step 4.8596 25.182 4.2855e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 19% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
13 R retirement_step 4.8986 24.911 3.2467e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 19% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
14 T tail 4.9646 24.463 2.0089e+08 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
15 R retirement_step 5.0396 24.174 1.1297e+08 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 21% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
16 R retirement_step 5.1026 23.941 6.6264e+07 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 24% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
